{
  "_comment": "Reference entry to merge into C:\\Users\\jesus\\.minimax\\mcp\\mcp.json. The actual installer (infra/install.sh) does this automatically; this file is documentation only.",
  "bash-mcp": {
    "url": "http://<WSL_IP>:54321/mcp/",
    "type": "streamable-http",
    "enabled": true,
    "configured": true,
    "description": "WSL bash executor — REQUIRED for any WSL command. Tools (v0.8.0): bash-mcp_run_command, bash-mcp_check_env, bash-mcp_list_binaries, bash-mcp_which, bash-mcp_status, bash-mcp_classify, bash-mcp_audit_read, bash-mcp_session_create, bash-mcp_session_run, bash-mcp_session_destroy, bash-mcp_session_list. DO NOT use `wsl -d ... -- bash -c \"...\"` from PowerShell — that path has quoting, UTF-16, and PATH bugs. Instead, call bash-mcp_run_command({command: \"...\"}). Safety: denylist (HARD + SOFT) + timeouts + output cap + audit log; pass dangerous=true to bypass SOFT denylist (HARD cannot be bypassed). Sessions: server-side cwd + env persistence across calls; process-lifetime only — destroy explicitly to free. v0.7.1: bash-mcp_audit_read transparently decompresses .jsonl.N.gz backups. v0.8: per-project cwd allowlists via .bash-mcp.toml (extend/replace modes, walk-up search, fail-soft on parse errors) — drop a TOML in your repo root to override the global allowlist for calls whose cwd lives under it."
  }
}